## Functional testing (agents)

Used by the **functional-test** skill after **implement**. The human keeps the dev server running; agents do **not** start/stop it unless this section says otherwise. UI runner depends on harness: Cursor integrated browser, Claude in Chrome (`--chrome`), Codex browser MCP if configured, else **Playwright** subagent. Screenshots land in the ticket `validation/` folder in Obsidian.

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Base URL (local) | FILL: e.g. `http://localhost:3000` |
| Health check | FILL: e.g. `curl -sf http://localhost:3000/api/health` |
| Playwright `storageState` (optional) | FILL: path, e.g. `.scratch/playwright/storageState.json` (gitignore) |
| Test auth env vars (names only) | FILL: e.g. `E2E_USER`, `E2E_PASSWORD` — never put values here |

If browser login is required and no storageState exists yet, use the **wizard** skill once; document the path above after capture.

For Surf tickets, validation artifacts go in the Obsidian vault (`Proyect/Tickets/{code}/validation/`), not in this repo: `report.md`, `manual-reproduction.md` (human copy of the same steps the agent ran), and screenshots.

