## Agent git rules

Defaults (override in the table or here if this repo differs):

- Work on **feature branches**; do not commit directly to protected branches unless the human explicitly asks.
- **Never push or merge** to testing, UAT, or production branches (or any row marked no above).
- **Push** only when the human explicitly asks. On a Surf ticket, “commit and push” is that permission. **Ticket done** says whether that push is also a done gate.
- **Pull requests:** target branch FILL: e.g. `dev`. Open or update a PR only when asked; branch must exist on remote first unless the human asked to push.

## Surf tickets (Blue Surf)

When working a ticket pulled with **bluesurf-ticket**:

- Commit subject ends with the ticket key in parentheses: FILL: e.g. `(PRY-123)`.
- Run **functional-test** after **implement**, in the same conversation.
- Mark the ticket done only under **Ticket done**.

## Ticket done

This section is the only definition of when an agent may run `npm run ticket-done` (delete the Obsidian ticket folder for this work item). **bluesurf-ticket** reads it after functional-test passes, when the human asks to mark the ticket done, and after a commit-and-push on that ticket.

Functional-test must already have passed. That gate lives in **bluesurf-ticket**; leave it out of the table.

Commit, push, and merge follow **Agent git rules**. They count toward ticket-done only when a row below says so.

